    "3.5",
    "3D scene or animation created with Bryce 4 3D modeling software; often used to create three-dimensional landscapes with realistic natural elements, such as hills, mountains, water, trees, clouds, sky, etc; may also be used to create basic 3D models of people or other objects. The company that developed Bryce 3D transitioned from Metacreations to Viewpoint for version 4.0. It was later bought by Corel, then by DAZ Productions. NOTE: BR4 files can be opened by Bryce version 4 or later. Windows DAZ 3D Bryce 7 Pro. Mac DAZ 3D Bryce 7 Pro.",
