    ["3d_image_files",
    ".PRIMITIVES",
    "World of Tanks 3D Model File",
    "2.3",
    "3D model file used by World of Tanks, a war game that features battles between tanks; contains information about a 3D model used in the game such as a tank, armored vehicle, or building. You can use the 3D Object Converter to convert PRIMITIVES files to a more common format such as the.3DS or.DXF file. You can then edit the format with an application that supports the format to which you converted the PRIMITIVES file. After making your changes you can convert it back to the PRIMITIVES format with the BigWorld Primitives Exporter and load it in the game. NOTE: The PRIMITIVES format was replaced by the.PRIMITIVES_PROCESSED format with the release of WoT 0.9.10. Windows Wargaming.net World of Tanks. 3D Object Converter.",
    "Windows Wargaming.net World of Tanks. 3D Object Converter.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".MP",
    "Maya PLE Project File",
    "2.2",
    "File used by MetaPost, a graphics-drawing language used for creating pictures in Encapsulated PostScript (.EPS) files and LaTeX documents (.TEX and.LTX files); may contain basic drawing statements or more advanced instructions for algorithmic drawing. The MetaPost system is often used for drawing diagrams in technical documents and academic journal papers. Since supports the automatic generation of formatted images in documents, it is commonly used for graphing data results as illustrations and figures in papers. NOTE: MetaPost is based off of the Metafont technology, which was created by Donald Knuth. Windows Texmaker. MetaPost Editor and Previewer. MetaGraf —  (Discontinued). Mac Texmaker. MetaPost Editor and Previewer. Linux Texmaker. MetaPost Editor and Previewer. MetaGraf —  (Discontinued). Project created with Maya Personal Learning Edition (PLE), a 3D modeling program developed for non-commercial use; similar to a.MA file, but saved in a non-commercial format with an identifying watermark. NOTE: MP files can be opened with Maya PLE, but cannot be opened with the commercial version of Maya. Windows Autodesk Maya PLE Mac Autodesk Maya PLE.",
    "Windows Texmaker. MetaPost Editor and Previewer. MetaGraf —  (Discontinued). Mac Texmaker. MetaPost Editor and Previewer. Linux Texmaker. MetaPost Editor and Previewer. MetaGraf —  (Discontinued). Windows Autodesk Maya PLE. Mac Autodesk Maya PLE.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".NSBTA",
    "Nintendo DS Texture Animation File",
    "2.2",
    "File used by Nintendo DS video games; contains data that specifies texture animation, such as a boost pad animation on a Super Mario Kart race track; enables the texture appearance to change without affecting the 3D geometry of the base model. NOTE: Model files (.NSBMD), textures (.NSBTX), and character animations (.NSBCA) are also used by Nintendo DS models. Windows MKDS Course ModifierFree.",
    "Windows MKDS Course Modifier.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".CGA",
    "Crytek Geometry Animation File",
    "2.0",
    "File created by the Crytek CryENGINE SDK, a program suite used for making 3D games; used for vehicle animations rather than character animations since it is not suited for skeletal bending parts that require skinned geometries; used with an animation (.ANM) file to animate the vehicle. NOTE: Characters are specified using.CHR files in the CryENGINE SDK. Windows Crytek CryENGINE SDK.",
    "Windows Crytek CryENGINE SDK.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".GLSLESF",
    "OpenGL ES Fragment Shader",
    "2.0",
    "A GLSLESF file is an OpenGL ES fragment shader. It contains fragment shading properties specified using the OpenGL Shading Language (GLSL). OpenGL ES uses GLSLESF files to produce colors and depth values for 3D graphics. OpenGL for Embedded Systems, or OpenGL ES, is an extension of the standard OpenGL API. It is used primarily to render 2D and 3D graphics on embedded systems such as smartphones, tablets, and video game consoles. However, it is also used in some desktop applications, such as Google Earth Pro. Like the standard version of OpenGL, OpenGL ES uses fragment shaders to render graphics with color, shadows, and other effects. These fragment shaders are plain text files that contain directives written in GLSL. While there is no standard file extension for OpenGL ES fragment shaders, they are sometimes saved with the.glslesf extension. NOTE: OpenGL fragment shaders are also saved as.FSH or.GLSL files. You can open and edit GLSLESF files with the tools included with the OpenGL SDK (multiplatform). You can also open and edit GLSLESF files Microsoft Visual Studio Code (multiplatform) or any other text or source code editor. Mac OpenGL SDK. Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Windows OpenGL SDK. Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Linux OpenGL SDK. Microsoft Visual Studio CodeFree.",
    "Mac OpenGL SDK. Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Windows OpenGL SDK. Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Linux OpenGL SDK. Microsoft Visual Studio Code.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".CHRPARAMS",
    "CryENGINE Character Parameters File",
    "2.0",
    "File created with the CryENGINE SDK, a program suite used for building 3D games; contains references to the character animation files (.CAF) as well as information about animation events for the character that can be invoked when programming the game. As of CryENGINE 3.3, the CHRPARAMS format replaces the use of.CAL,.IK, and.SETUP files. The information from these three file types is now consolidated into the CHRPARAMS format. Windows Crytek CryENGINE SDK.",
    "Windows Crytek CryENGINE SDK.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".EMCAM",
    "Mastercam Learning Edition Model",
    "2.0",
    "An EMCAM file is a 3D model created by CNC Software Mastercam Learning Edition, the free trial of Mastercam computer-aided design (CAD) software. It contains one or more objects with their 3D coordinates, levels, planes, and other information. Machinists often create and edit mechanical parts with Mastercam Learning Edition to produce physical copies of the part. EMCAM file open in CNC Software Mastercam Learning Edition 2023 CNC Mastercam is a widely-used CAD/CAM package that engineers and machinists use to design and produce mechanical components. CNC Software developed the Learning Edition of Mastercam for students, teachers, and professionals to be able to try the software before purchasing it. Since the Learning Edition of Mastercam does not allow you to save models in the default Mastercam format, CNC Software developed the EMCAM format. You can create an EMCAM file with Mastercam Learning Edition by selecting File → Save or Save As. After saving the model, you can close the file, then re-open it to continue modifying it. You can open an EMCAM file with CNC Mastercam Learning Edition in Windows by selecting File → Open. Windows CNC Software Mastercam Learning Edition.",
    "Windows CNC Software Mastercam Learning Edition.",
    "CNC Mastercam Learning Edition can convert EMCAM files to the following formats:.STL - Stereolithography File.3MF - 3D Manufacturing File.OBJ - Wavefront 3D Object File.AMF - Additive Manufacturing File."],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".VROID",
    "VRoid Studio Avatar",
    "2.0",
    "A VROID file is a 3D avatar created by pixiv VRoid Studio, an avatar creation program. It is saved in a proprietary format used only by VRoid Studio. Users typically export VROID files from VRoid Studio as.VRM files, for use with other programs. VROID file open in pixiv VRoid Studio VRoid Studio allows you to create a 3D avatar and export it in the VRM format, for use with VR programs that support the VRM 3D avatar standard. These avatars typically look like anime characters with stylized hair and clothes. Natively, VRoid Studio saves users avatars as VROID files. You can open a VROID file in VRoid Studio to edit the avatar it contains. (You cannot open VRM files in VRoid Studio.) By default, VRoid Studio saves users VROID files in the following directory: Windows: ~/​Users/​YourUserName/​Documents/​vroid/​avatars Mac: ~/​Users/​YourUserName/​vroid/​avatars. You can open a VROID file with VRoid Studio (Windows, Mac). To do so, select Open from VRoid Studios model selection screen. Then, navigate to and open your VROID file. Windows pixiv VRoid Studio. Mac pixiv VRoid StudioFree.",
    "Windows pixiv VRoid Studio. Mac pixiv VRoid Studio.",
    "You can use VRoid Studio to convert a VROID file to the following formats:.VRM - Virtual Reality Model FVP - pixivFACTORY 3D Printing File To do so, select the Upload button that appears in the programs upper-right corner. Then, select either Export as VRM or Export for 3D Printing."],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".IGMESH",
    "Indigo Renderer Mesh File",
    "2.0",
    "An IGMESH file contains mesh information in an object included in an Indigo Renderer 3D Scene (.IGS). It contains various mesh information, including an array of vertex positions, shading information, UV mappings, and materials used by the mesh. IGMESH files define shapes in scenes by providing a structural build (consisting of vertices, faces, and edges) of a 3D model. Indigo Renderer and Indigo RT are multiplatform 3D rendering applications primarily used by professional artists to generate photorealistic images. Indigo RT is similar to Indigo Renderer but offers fewer capabilities and is less expensive. Additionally, Indigo RT is available as a plugin for other 3D CAD software. Where to find IGMESH files You will likely encounter IGMESH files accompanying IGS files in a scene folder. The folder will likely be the same name as the IGS file but with _meshes appended. For example, if the IGS file is example_scene.igs, then the folder storing the IGMESH files will be named example_scene_meshes.igs. Typically, there are numerous IGMESH files in the folder, and their names begin with mesh, followed by a string of numbers. An example IGMESH file looks like this: mesh_7945098992065549788.igmesh. You should not attempt to open IGMESH files. Instead, Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer (multiplatform) and Indigo RT (multiplatform) reference the files when opening a scene. Windows Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT. Mac Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT. Linux Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT.",
    "Windows Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT. Mac Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT. Linux Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".HR2",
    "Poser Hair File",
    "2.0",
    "Contains character hair information, used by Poser, a 3D figure modeling program; may include either strand-based or transparency-mapped hair information; can be applied to various Poser 3D models. Poser was originally developed by Smith Micro, but was sold to Bondware in June 2019. Windows Bondware Poser. Mac Bondware Poser.",
    "Windows Bondware Poser. Mac Bondware Poser.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".DSI",
    "Double-Precision Spectral Image",
    "2.0",
    "File created by DAZ Studio, a program used for 3D character modeling; stores multiple image layers as a material file that can be applied to 3D objects; allows the source images (e.g.,.PNG or.JPG) to be combined while allowing each image to remain unmodified from its original state. Windows DAZ 3D DAZ Studio 4. Mac DAZ 3D DAZ Studio 4Free. A DSI file is an official Nintendo DSi game ROM issued by Nintendo. It contains a game downloaded from the Nintendo DSi Shop. DSI files can be used to play games on the Nintendo DSi and Nintendo 3DS, as well as in Nintendo DSi and 3DS emulators. The Nintendo DSi was the successor to the Nintendo DS and the predecessor to the Nintendo 3DS. The DSi and the 3DS allowed gamers to download a collection of games, commonly referred to as DSiWare, from the Nintendo DSi Shop and eShop. DSiWare games were saved in DSI files. In addition to allowing players to play downloaded games on their Nintendo devices, DSI files can be used to create unofficial ROMs that PC-based DSi and 3DS emulators, such as Citra, can open. To create an emulator-compatible ROM from a DSI file, gamers can use GodMode9 (Nintendo 3DS) or GodMode9i (Nintendo DSi). You can use GodMode9 (Nintendo 3DS) or GodMode9i (Nintendo DSi) to transform a DSI file into a Citra-compatible ROM. Then, you can use your new ROM to play the game your DSI file contains in Citra (cross-platform). Windows Citra. Mac Citra. Linux Citra. Android CitraFree. 3D image file created by Fryrender, a physics-based light simulator application used for photo-realistic rendering; stores a spectral map, which stores the radiances captured by the camera; used in the process of rendering the final lighting effects onto an image. DSI files are generated from a source.FRY scene file. NOTE: fryrender has been discontinued. Windows RandomControl fryrender.",
    "Windows DAZ 3D DAZ Studio 4. Mac DAZ 3D DAZ Studio 4. Windows Citra. Mac Citra. Linux Citra. Android Citra. Windows RandomControl fryrender.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".PREVIZ",
    "FrameForge Storyboard Studio Previsualization",
    "2.0",
    "A PREVIZ file is a 3D film storyboard created by FrameForge Storyboard Studio. It contains binary data that FrameForge translates into shots and scenes. PREVIZ files can be opened only in FrameForge Storyboard Studio. PREVIZ file open in FrameForge Storyboard Studio FrameForge Storyboard Studio is a Windows and Mac program that storyboard artists and other film professionals use to concept shots for movies. These 3D storyboards are referred to as previsualizations. FrameForge saves users previsualization projects as PREVIZ files. A user can open a PREVIZ file in FrameForge to see and play the shots it contains, and edit those shots as needed. Users can also export the storyboard a PREVIZ file contains as an.HTML file, a series of images, or a slideshow. NOTE: FrameForge Storyboard Studio uses a variety of related but slightly-distinct PREVIZ file formats. For example, a macOS user can save PREVIZ files in a Mac-only file format, a cross-platform file format, or a version 2 file format. You can open a PREVIZ file in FrameForge Storyboard Studio (Windows, Mac). To do so, select File → Open.. from the programs menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your PREVIZ file. Note that if your PREVIZ file was created on a different platform (e.g. you are a Windows user and your PREVIZ file was created on macOS), it may not open in your version of FrameForge Storyboard Studio. Windows FrameForge Storyboard Studio. Mac FrameForge Storyboard Studio.",
    "Windows FrameForge Storyboard Studio. Mac FrameForge Storyboard Studio.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".TMO",
    "3DCG Animation and Pose File",
    "2.0",
    "File created by 3D Custom Girl (3DCG), a program often used for creating virtual dancing characters for MikuMikuDance; saves pose (bone position) or animation information for a character and can be converted to a.VPD file, which is the format required by MikiMikuDance. NOTE: TMO files can be converted to MikuMikuDances VPD format using a program named tmo2vpd. Windows 3D Custom Girl tmo2vpd.",
    "Windows 3D Custom Girl tmo2vpd.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".PIGM",
    "Packed Indigo Renderer Material File",
    "2.0",
    "A PIGM file is a packed material (.IGM) used by Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer and Indigo RT, 3D visualization applications. It saves an IGM material in a.ZIP format, significantly reducing the material file size and making it more convenient to distribute materials online. Indigo Renderer is a 3D rendering application that allows artists to create photorealistic images. The software simulates the physics of light to generate images for various purposes, including architectural mockups and film special effects. Indigo Renderer is available as a standalone application or as a plugin for other 3D CAD programs. Additionally, Indigo RT is also a high-end 3D visualization application. It is similar to Indigo Renderer but offers fewer features and is less expensive. How to create a PIGM file with Indigo Renderer You can create a PIGM file with Indigo Renderer when saving a material you want to share or store. To create a PIGM file with Indigo Renderer, select File → New Material, choose File → Save Material As, then select Packed Indigo Material from the file type dropdown menu. You can open a PIGM file with Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer (multiplatform) and Indigo RT (multiplatform). For example, to open the file with Indigo Renderer, select File → Open. Since PIGM files are Zip-compressed, you can also change the.pigm file extension to.zip, then extract the IGM file stored in the archive with a Zip compression utility, such as File Explorer (Windows) or Apple Archive Utility (macOS). Windows Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT. Mac Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT. Linux Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT.",
    "Windows Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT. Mac Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT. Linux Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT.",
    "Indigo Renderer can convert PIGM files to various file types, including the following formats:.IGM - Indigo Renderer Material File.PNG - Adobe Illustrator Artwork.JPG - AutoCAD Drawing.TIFF - Drawing Exchange Format.EXR - IGES Drawing."],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".CAL",
    "CryENGINE Character Animation List",
    "2.0",
    "Calendar created by various Broderbund calendar design programs; contains dates and events, separated by months; may also include custom images for each month and user-defined formatting. Windows Broderbund The Print Shop. Broderbund PrintMaster 2020. Broderbund Calendar Creator. Mac Broderbund The Print Shop for Mac. Broderbund PrintMaster 2020. File created by 3ds Max, a three-dimensional modeling and animation application; contains adjustment values for a bipeds pose created while in the Adjust Talent Pose mode; used for adding pose information to the figures structure, which is saved in a.FIG file. NOTE: A biped is a two-footed figure, such as a human character. Windows Autodesk 3ds Max 2023. 1-bit (black and white) raster image; can be uncompressed or compressed using CCITT Group 4 compression; available in Type I and Type II versions, though Type I is more common. CALS stands for Continuous Acquisition and Life-cycle Support. The standard was developed by the U.S. Department of Defense as a means to electronically capture military documentation. Windows Adobe Photoshop 2023. CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. Newera Graphics Converter Pro. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023. File created using the CryENGINE SDK, an application suite used for developing 3D games; saves a list of all animation asset (.CAF) files used for character animation in the game. NOTE: In CryENGINE 3.3, CAL files were merged with.IK and.SETUP files into a single.CHRPARAMS file to simplify character animation configuration. Therefore, CAL files are no longer used. Windows Crytek CryENGINE SDK.",
    "Windows Broderbund The Print Shop. Broderbund PrintMaster 2020. Broderbund Calendar Creator. Mac Broderbund The Print Shop for Mac. Broderbund PrintMaster 2020. Windows Autodesk 3ds Max 2023. Windows Adobe Photoshop 2023. CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. Corel PaintShop Pro 2023. Canvas GFX Canvas X Pro. Newera Graphics Converter Pro. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023. Windows Crytek CryENGINE SDK.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".TGO",
    "Terragen Object File",
    "2.0",
    "Object created by Terragen, a landscape generation program; contains a three dimensional object and any attached nodes; similar to the.OBJ file but in the Terragen native format; objects built into Terragen include grass clumps, landmarks, rocks, and spheres. To import a TGO file, select File → Import Object → Terragen Object (.tgo), choose your save location, verify that the File Format is TGO, and click Open. Mac Planetside Software Terragen. Windows Planetside Software Terragen.",
    "Mac Planetside Software Terragen. Windows Planetside Software Terragen.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".DBC",
    "DAZ Brick Camera File",
    "2.0",
    "A DBC file is a database created with Visual FoxPro, a database development system. It contains a database saved in the Database Container (DBC) format. Visual FoxPro is used to manage large volumes of data for desktop, distributed client, client/server, rich client, and web database applications. Visual FoxPro has been discontinued. The last version (9) was released in 2004 and last updated in 2007. Windows Microsoft Visual FoxPro. Aryson DBF Recovery. 3D image shader file created by DAZ Studio, an application used for 3D modeling; saves a shader network that specifies how an object is shaded when viewed with a certain camera in the scene; can be opened and edited from the Shader Mixer view (Window → Tabs → Shader Mixer) by selecting File → Open Shader... Windows DAZ 3D DAZ Studio 4. Mac DAZ 3D DAZ Studio 4Free.",
    "Windows Microsoft Visual FoxPro. Aryson DBF Recovery. Windows DAZ 3D DAZ Studio 4. Mac DAZ 3D DAZ Studio 4.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".STC",
    "Shade to Manga Studio File",
    "2.0",
    "Connection file created by Contribute, an Adobe program used for website development and publishing; saves the remote host, the connection protocol (e.g., FTP, SFTP, etc.) and the username; enables users to reuse connection information and distribute it among website developers. When you double-click an STC file, Contribute opens a connection to the remote server and shows the remote files. Windows Adobe Contribute 6.5 —  (Discontinued). Trial Mac Adobe Contribute 6.5 —  (Discontinued). Trial. Data file used by Celestia, a cross-platform application used to create 3D simulations of the universe; stores instructions for drawing stars in the universe; comprises part of the overall universe database when the program loads. Celestia automatically load an STC file on startup if the file is in the correct location. Custom STC,.DSC, and.SSC catalog files must be located within the /​extras-standard/​ subdirectory of the Celestia installation. Windows Celestia. Mac Celestia. Linux CelestiaFree. Template for creating a new spreadsheet file; originally used by the older StarOffice software and still supported by the more recent Apache OpenOffice; created by the Calc program included with StarOffice. Apache OpenOffice now uses the.OTS OpenDocument format for storing spreadsheet templates. NOTE: Apache OpenOffice was formerly known as OpenOffice.org. Windows OpenOffice Calc. LibreOffice. Mac OpenOffice Calc. Planamesa NeoOffice. LibreOffice. Linux OpenOffice Calc. LibreOfficeFree. 3D model exported from a Shade 3D model to a format recognized by Manga Studio; created by the Shade to Manga Studio plug-in, which is included with Manga Studio EX; can be imported into comic books designed with Manga Studio. STC files generally include models of characters used in comics. Manga Studio became Clip Studio Paint in 2015. It is also known as ComicStudio in Japan. Windows CELSYS Clip Studio Paint Pro. Mac CELSYS Clip Studio Paint Pro. Theme file used by Siemens mobile phones; stored within a.SDT global theme file and contains XML markup that specifies how the theme looks and what sounds to play; can be viewed with any text editor. Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor.",
    "Windows Adobe Contribute 6.5 —  (Discontinued). Trial. Mac Adobe Contribute 6.5 —  (Discontinued). Trial. Windows Celestia. Mac Celestia. Linux Celestia. Windows OpenOffice Calc. LibreOffice. Mac OpenOffice Calc. Planamesa NeoOffice. LibreOffice. Linux OpenOffice Calc. LibreOffice. Windows CELSYS Clip Studio Paint Pro. Mac CELSYS Clip Studio Paint Pro. Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".VAC",
    "MikuMikuDance Accessory Settings File",
    "2.0",
    "Computer Algebra kit; contains a large set of classes for polynomial computing and arbitrary precision integer arithmetic. Windows Portable Object Compiler or other C compiler Mac Portable Object Compiler or other C compiler. 3D model file used by MikuMikuDance, a modeling program and music and dance synchronization game; contains coordinate and rotation settings for a 3D model accessory (.X file), such as clothing or hair; used for automatically placing accessories on a 3D model. Windows MikuMikuDanceFree.",
    "Windows Portable Object Compiler or other C compiler. Mac Portable Object Compiler or other C compiler. Windows MikuMikuDance.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".FPE",
    "FPS Creator Entity File",
    "2.0",
    "File used by FPS Creator, a program used to create First Person Shooter (FPS) games; contains text properties for the display of an in-game entity, such as its description, geometry, lighting effects, model filename, and texture filename; used with other files to package a model for a game. Windows The Game Creators FPS CreatorFree. An FPE file is a document created by. PDF Editor, a program used to create.PDF files. It contains formatted text, images, shapes, and page formatting. FPE files are typically used for creating business documents and personal invitations and newsletters. FPE file open in. PDF Editor You can create an FPE file in. PDF Editor by selecting File → New and save it by selecting File → Save or Save As.. After you are done editing the FPE file, you can export it as a PDF file by selecting File → Create PDF... PDF Editor comes with various of editing features, such as the ability to insert text, images, and shapes or modify font color and size. When you create your document you will save it as an FPE file. Then, once you make all your modifications you can save it as a PDF file. NOTE:. PDF Editor is discontinued. Windows. PDF Editor —  (Discontinued).",
    "Windows The Game Creators FPS Creator. Windows. PDF Editor —  (Discontinued).",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".3DV",
    "3D VRML World",
    "2.0",
    "3D virtual reality world saved in the VRML format; contains scenes and objects that make up a virtual world; allows users to walk through virtual areas, such as buildings and various landscapes. Windows IMSI TurboCAD Pro. Mac IMSI TurboCAD Deluxe.",
    "Windows IMSI TurboCAD Pro. Mac IMSI TurboCAD Deluxe.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".XAF",
    "Cal3D XML Animation File",
    "2.0",
    "XML file created by the 3ds Max modeling and animation software; contains motion information for a biped, which is a model with two-feet; enables modelers to accurately capture human and creature movements for video games, movies, and other 3D animations. XAF files can be reused across multiple biped models. They can also be included in a 3ds Max Motion Mixer mix (.MIX file), which allows animators to composite an animation on a multi-track timeline. Windows Autodesk 3ds Max 2023. File created by the Affirm Transcript Editor, a program used for creating deposition transcripts during legal proceedings; stores rich text and contains the verbal testimony of a witness recorded out of the courtroom. XAF files enable lawyers to store digital evidence during litigation. NOTE: Web Depo Affirm Transcript Editor has been discontinued and is no longer available for download. Windows Web Depo Affirm Transcript Editor. 3D animation file used by Cal3D, an open source toolkit used for character animation; stores bone movements for the models skeleton, which is specified in a.CSF or.XSF file; used for creating realistic human motions. XAF files store animation data in an XML format, but Cal3D animation data can also be stored in a binary format using.CAF files. Windows Cal3dViewer. Cal3d2ogre. Linux Cal3DFree.",
    "Windows Autodesk 3ds Max 2023. Windows Web Depo Affirm Transcript Editor. Windows Cal3dViewer. Cal3d2ogre. Linux Cal3D.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".XSF",
    "Cal3D XML Skeleton File",
    "2.0",
    "File used by InfoPath, a program used for creating forms; specifies the content, properties, and structure of the form template (.XSN file); stored as one of the files inside of the XSN template; adheres to the InfoPath XSF schema (an.XSD file) published by Microsoft. Most of the time XSF files are generated and maintained automatically by the InfoPath software. However, sometimes form developers manually edit XSF files to extend the functionality of the form templates. Windows Microsoft InfoPath. Three-dimensional model file created using Cal3D, an open source character animation program; contains parent to child relationships between the characters skeletal bones (torso, legs, arms, etc); used for creating character motion. XSF files store the skeleton data using XMl formatting, whereas Cal3D skeleton.CSF files use a binary format. Windows Cal3dViewer. Cal3d2ogre. Linux Cal3DFree.",
    "Windows Microsoft InfoPath. Windows Cal3dViewer. Cal3d2ogre. Linux Cal3D.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".IGM",
    "Indigo Renderer Material File",
    "2.0",
    "An IGM file is a material created by Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer, an app for generating photorealistic 3D images. It stores the graphical properties of a material in the XML standard that gives the surface of a 3D object a realistic appearance, such as that of metal, wood, plastic, brick, or liquid. IGM files may be included as part of an Indigo Renderer scene (.IGS file). IGM file open in Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer 4 Indigo Renderer is a multiplatform 3D rendering application that allows professional artists to create photorealistic images. Artists may create architectural mockups, video game scenes, film special effects, and more. The software is available as a standalone application or as a plugin for other 3D CAD programs. How to create an IGM file with Indigo Renderer You can create an IGM file with Indigo Renderer when saving a material. To create an IGM file with Indigo Renderer, select File → New Material, then choose File → Save Material or Save Material As. While many artists create IGM files from scratch. You can also download IGM files from Indigo Renderers website for free. Additionally, if you want to share an IGM file, you can compress it in the.PIGM format, which reduces the size to make it easier to store or transfer. You can open an IGM file with Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer (multiplatform) and Indigo RT (multiplatform). For example, to open the file with Indigo Renderer, select File → Open. Windows Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT. Mac Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT. Linux Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT.",
    "Windows Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT. Mac Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT. Linux Glare Technologies Indigo Renderer. Glare Technologies Indigo RT.",
    "Indigo Renderer can convert IGM files to various file types, including the following formats:.PIGM - Packaged Indigo Renderer Material File.PNG - Adobe Illustrator Artwork.JPG - AutoCAD Drawing.TIFF - Drawing Exchange Format.EXR - IGES Drawing."],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".CSF",
    "Cal3D Binary Skeleton File",
    "2.0",
    "A CSF file is a color management settings file used by Adobe Photoshop, InDesign, and Illustrator. It contains policies for color images, such as web graphic color definitions, ColorSync colors, prepress colors for different countries, and other color settings. CSF files are used for achieving color consistency between images and prints. NOTE: CSF files can be shared between Photoshop, InDesign, and Illustrator. They may also be managed using the Adobe Bridge application. Windows Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe InDesign 2023. Adobe Illustrator 2023. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe InDesign 2023. Adobe Illustrator 2023. Coordinate system file used by GeoMedia, a GIS application used to analyze geographic information and produce maps; contains the coordinate system for an output data file that has no system in place; includes the base storage type, which is either Geographic, Projection, or Geocentric, of the coordinate system. A CSF file is used to define the coordinate system of input data with no specified coordinate system. It is created when the input data is exported to an output data format, such as the MicroStation V7 format. When it is exported, the CSF file is generated in the same location as the output file(s). NOTE: To create or edit a CSF file, use the Define Coordinate System File utility included with the GeoMedia software. ExportDGN.csf - The CSF file bear this name if multiple output files are produced. If only one output file is produced, the CSF file will be named with the same name as the output file. Windows Intergraph GeoMedia —  (Discontinued). Secure 2D image format that is a replica of the source image file; can embed print and watermark banners, limit printing and copying, and may include an expiration date; may also be password-protected; used for safe file sharing. Windows Informative Graphics Brava! Reader. 3D skeleton file created using Cal3D open source character animation software; stores a list of bones in the form of a parent to child relationship; used by the animation component for creating head, torso, leg, arm, and hand movements. Cal3D skeleton files can also be expressed in an XML form using.XSF files. Windows Cal3dViewer. Cal3d2ogre. Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Mac Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Linux Cal3DFree.",
    "Windows Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe InDesign 2023. Adobe Illustrator 2023. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023. Adobe InDesign 2023. Adobe Illustrator 2023. Windows Intergraph GeoMedia —  (Discontinued). Windows Informative Graphics Brava! Reader. Windows Cal3dViewer. Cal3d2ogre. Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Mac Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Linux Cal3D.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".MCX-8",
    "Mastercam X8 Model",
    "2.0",
    "An MCX-8 file is a 3D model created by Mastercam X8, a computer-aided design (CAD) and computer-aided manufacturing (CAM) application. It is a representation of a mechanical part, which machinists use to produce a physical copy of that part. You can open MCX-8 files in Mastercam. From within Mastercam, you can convert MCX-8 files to.IGS or.SPT files, for use in other CAD and CAM applications. In 1983, CNC Software released the first version of Mastercam. Mastercam was one of the first CAD and CAM applications that allowed machinists and engineers to model mechanical parts and help automate part production. Over the years, CNC Software has released many subsequent versions of Mastercam. In 2014, CNC Software released Mastercam X8. Mastercam X8 saved users 3D part designs as MCX-8 files. In 2019, CNC Software discontinued Mastercam X8, suggesting that users should upgrade to the then-current version of Mastercam, Mastercam 2020. However, current versions of Mastercam can still open MCX-8 files. You can open an MCX-8 file in CNC Software Mastercam (Windows). If you attempt to resave your MCX-8 file, youll likely be asked to save it in Mastercams current 3D model file format. Windows CNC Software Mastercam.",
    "Windows CNC Software Mastercam.",
    "?"],
    ["3d_image_files",
    ".CAF",
    "Cal3D Binary Animation File",
    "1.8",
    "A CAF file is an audio file saved in the Core Audio Format (CAF), a digital audio format based on Apples Core Audio technology. It stores audio data, text annotations, markers, channel layouts, and other information. CAF files are similar to.AIFF and.WAVE files, but do not have a 4GB size limit and can store any number of audio channels. CAF file open in VideoLAN VLC media player 3 The CAF file structure includes a file header that stores information about the file type and CAF version and is followed by multiple data chunks. Two chunks always present in CAF files are the 1) Audio Data chunk, which contains the audio data, and the 2) Audio Description chunk, which contains information that specifies the audio data format. Other types of chunks include the following: Channel Layout - Required for CAF files with more than one audio channel; describes the role of each channel in the file. Information - Stores text about the audio data, which includes the title and artist. Edit Comments - Contains time-stamped comments added when the CAF data is edited. Instrument - Stores descriptive information about audio data needed when the audio is used by a sampler or played as an instrument. NOTE: For more information about CAF, view Apples documentation. You can open CAF files with various audio players, including QuickTime Player 7 and later (included with macOS), VideoLAN VLC media player (multiplatform), Audacity (multiplatform), and NCH WavePad (multiplatform). The CAF audio format is supported by Mac OS X (10.4 and later) applications that incorporate the Core Audio API. The format is also supported by iOS, beginning with version 5.0. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. VideoLAN VLC media playerer GoldWave. Audacity. NCH WavePad. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Apple GarageBand Included with OS. Apple Logic Pro. Apple Final Cut Express —  (Discontinued). Apple Final Cut Pro. VideoLAN VLC media player. ShedWorx Smart Converter. Audacity. NCH WavePad. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. AudacityFree. File created by the CryENGINE SDK, an application suite used for making PC and console games; contains character animation data that was compiled from a.CHR character file using a.CBA compiler specification file. CAF files are used as intermediate compilation files before building the database animation (.DBA) file, which is suitable for use in the final game deliverable. Windows Crytek CryENGINE SDK. Gradebook file created by Class Action Gradebook, a program used for organizing classroom information; may contain student information, seating arrangements, homework assignments, awarded grades, and other class data. CAF files are used for managing gradebook data and for printing reports. Teachers can generate reports such as classroom grade summaries, individual student reports, parent letters, and class and assignment graphs. Each report can be customized. NOTE: CAF files are created by the Secondary and College editions of Class Action Gradebook. Windows CalEd Class Action Gradebook —  (Discontinued). A CAF file is a catalog created by the Cathy media cataloging tool. It contains an indexed catalog of media files that users can search through within Cathy. CAF files can be shared with other Cathy users to allow them to browse your media collection. Cathy is a free media cataloging program that music and movie enthusiasts can use to catalog the CDs, DVDs,.MP3s,.MP4s, and other media that they own. When a user saves a catalog within Cathy, it is saved as a CAF file. After creating a CAF catalog, users can search the catalog by filename, the date a file was created, or file size. Sometimes, Cathy users share their CAF catalogs with others, allowing those users to peruse their media collection. Note that sharing your CAF catalog with someone wont allow that person to actually play your media. However, it will allow you to compare the pieces of media you own (and maybe, inspire you to swap some files). You can open a CAF file in Cathy. To do so, place your CAF file in the same directory as your Cathy.exe file. Then, open Cathy. Your CAF catalog will appear in Cathy. Windows CathyFree. Three-dimensional animation file used by Cal3D, a free toolkit used for character modeling and animation; contains motion settings for the models skeleton; specifies rotations and movements for the models bones over time. CAF files are used to give characters realistic human motions. They can specify animations for walking, running, or various other movements. NOTE: Cal3D animation files can also be expressed in an XML format using.XAF files. Windows Cal3dViewer. Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Mac Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Linux Cal3DFree.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. VideoLAN VLC media playerer GoldWave. Audacity. NCH WavePad. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Apple GarageBand Included with OS. Apple Logic Pro. Apple Final Cut Express —  (Discontinued). Apple Final Cut Pro. VideoLAN VLC media player. ShedWorx Smart Converter. Audacity. NCH WavePad. Linux VideoLAN VLC media player. Audacity. Windows Crytek CryENGINE SDK. Windows CalEd Class Action Gradebook —  (Discontinued). Windows Cathy. Windows Cal3dViewer. Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Mac Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Linux Cal3D.",
    "?"],
